[size=5]Description[/size]
Got a spare weapon or supplies you no longer need? Dismantle lets you recover useful components through the inventory's [b]Dispose[/b] action.

The aim is to keep survival challenging while giving you more options when bad loot luck leaves you short on ammo, weapons or crafting ingredients. Try salvaging Alcohol from a looted Molotov, or recover Cans from a whole stack of food in one go. It's intended as a small quality-of-life improvement that stays close to the game's existing balance.

Use Dispose as usual, including the quantity or confirmation prompt. The button still says "Dispose", and any recovered items go straight into your inventory with the game's usual "added to inventory" popup.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Canned food and water:[/b] recover the empty Can or Plastic Bottle, one for each item disposed.
[*][b]Bandages:[/b] get 1 Rag back. [b]Batteries:[/b] have a 50% chance to give 1 Electronics each.
[*][b]Craftable weapons, attachments and crafting parts:[/b] recover one ingredient from their recipe, chosen at random. A weapon that can only be repaired (not crafted) gives Scrap or its weapon parts instead.
[*][b]Guns without a crafting recipe:[/b] get 1 Scrap (90%) or 1 Firearm Parts (10%). Metal melee weapons without a recipe give 1 Scrap (95%) or 1 Melee Parts (5%).
[*][b]Attachments without a crafting recipe:[/b] get 1 Scrap.
[*][b]Molotovs and improvised bombs:[/b] have a chance to return Alcohol, Explosives or other parts, depending on the throwable.
[/list]

Some items still give nothing, including a plain Bat or Board, ammo, and non-craftable throwables such as Grenades. Batteries and improvised throwables can also return nothing if the salvage chance fails. The item is still removed when you dispose of it.

[url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlsa/tlsa-dismantle/blob/main/docs/dismantle-recipes.md][b]Full dismantling recipes and salvage chances[/b][/url]
See the recipe guide for item-by-item returns and examples of disposing of a whole stack.

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx for The Last Stand: Aftermath[/url]. Install it first.
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path examples:
[list]
[*]Steam: [code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\Dismantle.dll[/code]
[*]Epic: [code]C:\Program Files\Epic Games\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\Dismantle.dll[/code]
[/list]
[/list]

[b]Example:[/b] Dispose of a non-craftable attachment to recover 1 Scrap.

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete Dismantle.dll from the BepInEx\plugins folder.

